ASoC: rockchip: spdif: add the rk3568 compatible

The rk3568 SPDIF transmitter is the same rk3366-class block (no GRF
preratio register, 10 MHz mclk), so it only needs its compatible string
in the match table - this is exactly what upstream did in v5.10
(commit "ASoC: rockchip: add support for rk3568").

Needed by the JP TV Box 3566 optical output (spdif@fe460000 in
rk3568.dtsi, which is already described with compatible
"rockchip,rk3568-spdif").

--- a/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_spdif.c
+++ b/sound/soc/rockchip/rockchip_spdif.c
@@ -58,6 +58,8 @@
 	  .data = (void *)RK_SPDIF_RK3366 },
 	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rk3399-spdif",
 	  .data = (void *)RK_SPDIF_RK3366 },
+	{ .compatible = "rockchip,rk3568-spdif",
+	  .data = (void *)RK_SPDIF_RK3366 },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, rk_spdif_match);
